ry of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"aretas_297","name":"Aretas","also":"","summary":"The father-in-law of Herod Antipas, and king of Arabia Petraea. His daughter returned to him on the occasion of her husband’s entering into an adulterous alliance with Herodias, the wife of Herod-Philip, his half-brother (Luke 3:19, 20; Mark 6:17; Matt. 14:3).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[32]}],"places":[{"id":"macedonia_747","name":"Macedonia","kind":"Region","lat":40.73292,"lon":22.9352,"summary":"In New Testament times, was a Roman province lying north of Greece. It was governed by a propraetor with the title of proconsul. Paul was summoned by the vision of the “man of Macedonia” to preach the gospel there (Acts 16:9).","verses":21,"v":[9]},{"id":"achaia_16","name":"Achaia","kind":"Region","lat":37.5,"lon":22.5,"summary":"The name originally of a narrow strip of territory in Greece, on the north-west of the Peloponnesus. Subsequently it was applied by the Romans to the whole Peloponnesus, now called the Morea, and the south of Greece.","verses":10,"v":[10]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[32]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3785,3785,430,430,430,430,430,5100,3398,1473,1473,877,235,430,430,430,430,430],[2206,2206,2206,2206,4771,2316,2316,2316,2205,1063,718,718,4771,1520,1520,435,3936,3936,3936,53,53,53,3933,5547,5547],[5399,5399,5399,1161,4459,4459,5613,2096,1818,1818,1722,3588,3789,3834,4771,3540,5351,5351,5351,5351,575,3588,572,2532,54,54,1519,5547],[1063,1487,3588,2064,2784,2784,2424,2424,243,3739,3739,3739,2784,2784,2228,2228,2983,2983,2087,2087,4151,3739,3739,3739,2983,2983,2228,2087,2087,2098,3739,3739,3739,1209,1209,430,430,430,430,430,2573,2573],[3049,30